{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch","id":793530,"title":"Which Legacies do you want in the post-release batch?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-27T05:38:06-08:00","id":793530,"title":"Which Legacies do you want in the post-release batch?","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> So, Mage is in layout now, which means release is edging ever-closer. I'm also 3000 words off having (for the first time in two years) no contracted writing to do for other Developers, so I've been planning some bits and pieces that will accompany second edition.<br /> <br /> One of those is a set of four Legacies, so that you have five of them. And I am having trouble deciding on what three of them should be.<br /> <br /> To clarify:<br /> <br /> The Eleventh Question (Moros or Guardians/Mysterium) are in the 2e core. I want to have at least one Legacy for each Path, and preferably for each Order, available as examples.<br /> <br /> I have already converted the Sisterhood of the Blessed (Acanthus or Silver Ladder/Seers) because I needed it for my own Chronicle.<br /> <br /> So!<br /> <br /> Out of the remaining 93 published Legacies, we need a Mastigos one, an Obrimos one, and a Thyrsus one. Preferably with some combination of the Arrow, Council, and Mysterium as the Orders. Does anyone have any requests?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T05:41:28-08:00","id":793531,"title":"","content":"Oh, right! Also - no Left Handed ones. These are meant to be playable. And I'm already doing the Tremere in the <i>other</i> early thing, which will be a mechanics update for Left Hand Path.<br /> <br /> I'm edging toward doing the Claviclarius/Bene Ashmedai as an example of a Legacy that split, because 2e's Legacy mechanics are better able to model such things than 1e was, and I'm missing a Mastigos one anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T05:53:15-08:00","id":793534,"title":"","content":"I'm kind of actually curious of why the Clavicularius/Bene Ashmedai as an example: to me they always read like that they had a &quot;mythological&quot; common ancenstry, but weren't really related at all.<br /> <br /> On the other hand the Sisterhood of the Blessed were the ones with an explicit Legacy split like what I think you're talking about, the one that became the Reality Makers. I also remember something similar in Keys of the Supernal Tarot, where one example character was a Clavicularius who had diverged from his Legacy by developing a different 2nd Attainment.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, legacies<br /> <br /> Obrimos Mysterium: Daksha. Gotta think a bit about the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","user":"BlueBiscuit","date":". 12-27-2015, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T06:19:50-08:00","id":793538,"title":"","content":"The Dreamspeakers (Thyrsus/Council) feel iconic to me, in the way that they invite exploration of the Anima Mundi and raise questions and considerations about its nature and that of the inhabitants.<br /> <br /> The combination of the Claviclarius and Bene Ashmedai sounds excellent; I remember proposing the latter as something for a fellow player's character to look into down the road of advancement and character development.<br /> <br /> It could be interesting to see how Awakening 2e's interpretation of reach and grasp translates the Quiescent from Mage Noir. They've always struck me as an engaging challenge for character concepts \u2013 not necessarily the easiest to fit into, but the kind that's appealing to try for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T06:20:48-08:00","id":793540,"title":"","content":"I support Clavicularius and Bene Ashmedai for Mastigos. As for the remaining two...<br /> <br /> Obrimos: Eyes of Ain Soph for Mysterium and Prime goodness (Mysterium, cannot check page number right now).<br /> <br /> Thyrsus: Imagineers for Free Council and a somewhat different take on Spirit (Free Council, cannot check page numbers right now).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T06:42:39-08:00","id":793544,"title":"","content":"I think a good idea would be to focus on very characteristic legacies on one hand and on the ones that are problematic to convert on the other (like the ones with various Arcana all over the place). So the Clavicularis/Bene Ashmedai seem like a good fit, as their pretty iconic and their atainments might be somewhat wonky to convert. Another option would be to choose legacies that suffered from somewhat poor write ups.<br /> <br /> As for the ones I'd like to see.<br /> <br /> Obrimos/Free Council: Transhuman Engineers, always liked them but their attainments seemed... not very transhuman and slightly boring. Merging humans with technology via... making their smartphones not need batteries. Huh.<br /> <br /> The Forge Masters would propably need some changes with enchanting items becoming now an attainment at all, and are very Moros in theme.<br /> <br /> Most of my favorite legacies where Acanthus though but seems like you have a pick for that already. However with the new Acanthus writeup some of them don't feel very much Acanthus so maybe you could reimagine one of those with a new path ? <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T06:45:27-08:00","id":793545,"title":"","content":"I agree with at least Clavicularius for the Mastigos one. In the same vein I will add other Legacies which I feel are iconic and that I have seen chosen by players more than once. Since I am not really able to pick favorites I will list more than three, but these are all Legacies that see play often in my games and LARP. Hopefully that helps.<br /> <br /> Brotherhood of the Demon Wind / Perfected Adept: These combat oriented Legacies are often part of the Adamantine Arrow in my games. Easy to understand and reference, they are simple player choices. Between these too I think the Brotherhood is the cooler one.<br /> <br /> Keepers of the Covenant: The Hierarch and other important PCs and NPCs are part of this Legacy. A good update since this Spirit-based legacy would get to explore the new Ephemeral systems from GMC and fits with the new Thyrsus ideal as a man-in-the-middle.<br /> <br /> Cryptologos: While this Legacy is currently attached to Mastigos, I've always felt it also plays well with Obrimos. My girlfriend plays an Obrimos hyperactive FC linguist Cryptologos with an Obsession on discovering Truths devised by ancient and modern cultures, through etymology and grammar.<br /> <br /> Pygmalian Society / Sisterhood of the Blessed: Good Acanthus fits and also two Legacies which are related. The Sisterhood has come up a little more often. Unfortunately Sisterhood are also SL, so if I had to choose between these two I would choose the Keepers of the Covenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T06:52:34-08:00","id":793549,"title":"","content":"I'll put in a couple of suggestions:<br /> <br /> Everyone tends to love the goetic Mind Mastigos legacies, but I would personally love to see the Reality Stalkers (Mysterium). With the move away from city-locked assumptions regarding cabal operations and a move towards more regional/global focus I can see them getting more love,<br /> <br /> The second one I would love to see is the Katsinam Suukya for the Thysus from Summoners. I love the way they Legacy opens up the concepts of spirit guides/shamans for wider and more modern interpretations. Just last night I was working on a character concept for a young Mohawk girl who was in New York City with her skyscraper ironworker father on 9/11 who's Awakening started when she felt the spirit of the first tower die and finished when the second tower died. Since 9/11 she has studied to be an architect and joined the Katsinam Suukya with the spirit guide of Skyscraper (a modern take on Community - if I was to time jump her 200 years in the future her spirit guide would probably be Archology).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3385-ckobbe","name":"ckobbe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T06:57:44-08:00","id":793550,"title":"","content":"I support Perfected Adepts for the Arrow and Obrimos. There aren't many Arrow Right-Handed legacies (3: Perfected Adept, Awakening Gambit, and Brotherhood of the Demon Wind), and I feel that the Acanthus and Mastigos have better legacies tied to them in other Orders (such as the Clavicularius).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T07:05:19-08:00","id":793551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=793531#post793531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm edging toward doing the Claviclarius/Bene Ashmedai as an example of a Legacy that split, because 2e's Legacy mechanics are better able to model such things than 1e was, and I'm missing a Mastigos one anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to vote for the Sphinxes, but a look at the Clavicularius/Bene Ashmedai split sounds really interesting, especially since it seems like the Bene Ashmedai will need a significant overhaul with the changes to Goetia/Spirits. <br /> <br /> For the Obrimos, I'll vote for the Tamers of Fire. They emphasize a lot of the Obrimos themes and they have strong Arrow leanings. <br /> <br /> I guess that leaves the Dreamspeakers for the Thyrsus/Free Council Legacy. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T07:12:00-08:00","id":793555,"title":"","content":"I'll third Dreamspeakers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T07:40:39-08:00","id":793564,"title":"","content":"Blank Badges are iconic Free Councillors, and the legacy is awesome, but the mechanics are a complete mess.<br /> <br /> They have no primary arcana, and do the things they do with Mind affect belief (Something that's no longer relevant in 2e) or is it some other esoteric use of the Mind arcana that we're not aware of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T07:44:38-08:00","id":793565,"title":"","content":"I agree with Dreamspeakers as Thyrsus / Free Council one group - nothing say more as to Libertines change on &quot;we are cultural mages&quot; as putting ancient Nameless Shamans as foundation for this new group.<br /> <br /> I also second Eyes of Ain Soph for Obrimos / Mysterium as it shows both most important changes in those two groups - mainly looking for &quot;secret laws&quot; and bieliving magic is Egregore of Living Mysteries.<br /> <br /> As to third one, I would point Brotherhood of the Demon Wind as Mastigos / Adamantine Arrow one, just because we need cool Arrow Legacy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If Mastigos one would goes for Clavicularis and Bene Ashmedai, I would then point Forge Masters as Moros / Adamantine Arrow + Free Council group, showing new Enhancement mechanics and maybe pointing to Perfected Alloys - Arrow group focused on &quot;perfection&quot; rather than combat is also needed.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T08:08:06-08:00","id":793573,"title":"","content":"The Quiescent were the highlight of the book that got me into Mage. I'd love to see them come back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T08:12:35-08:00","id":793576,"title":"","content":"Brotherhood of the Demon Wind (Mastigos, Arrow)<br /> Dreamspeakers (Thyrsus , Free Council)<br /> I would say Perfected Adept for Obrimos but its not Mysterium.<br /> <br /> Also, no seers of the throne?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T08:17:15-08:00","id":793578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=793576#post793576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, no seers of the throne?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sisterhood of the Blessed is also for Seers in 2e, check Dave's initial post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T08:21:20-08:00","id":793581,"title":"","content":"I definitely like seeing a new Clavicularius/Bene Ashmedai example in the new system.<br /> <br /> Mmm... coming up with one for the Arrow is really difficult, especially since you've got your Acanthus and you're leaning towards a Mastigos legacy. The only current example of an Arrow legacy not using one of those paths and not left handed is the Perfected Adept, which admittedly does fulfill the Obrimos slot, but which is also kind of dull; then again, under the new system, it could become something far more impressive. That said... if you're already making some alterations to some legacies (i.e. making the 11 Q not just GoV), could you change the Whipping Boys or the Daksha into an Arrow Legacy (in addition to what they now are), which would then give the Obrimos something as well? Both of those are definitely on my list of Legacies I want to see updated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T08:27:00-08:00","id":793586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=793564#post793564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blank Badges are iconic Free Councillors, and the legacy is awesome, but the mechanics are a complete mess.<br /> <br /> They have no primary arcana, and do the things they do with Mind affect belief (Something that's no longer relevant in 2e) or is it some other esoteric use of the Mind arcana that we're not aware of?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah yes I'd love to see a new write up for the Blanks. Another issue is that with the new path write ups don't feel really Acanthus right now (more like Mastigos for me)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T08:41:12-08:00","id":793595,"title":"","content":"There is a certain dearth of Arrow Legacies. However, there are Legacies not officially assigned to any Order, which could fit like a glove. I'm thinking about Fallen Pillar, Liberatores, Tamers of Fire, Whipping Boys and possibly others. This also applies to other Orders. I'm officially lobbying for them to be considered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T08:57:28-08:00","id":793600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=793595#post793595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a certain dearth of Arrow Legacies. However, there are Legacies not officially assigned to any Order, which could fit like a glove. I'm thinking about Fallen Pillar, Liberatores, Tamers of Fire, Whipping Boys and possibly others. This also applies to other Orders. I'm officially lobbying for them to be considered.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, all three of those could be Arrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T09:02:13-08:00","id":793602,"title":"","content":"For Obrimos, I would love to see the Perfected Adepts (Adamantine Arrow) or the Ascended Adepts. The latter could also be used as a good example of converting merits to Attainments.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T09:09:26-08:00","id":793608,"title":"","content":"Forge Masters and the Brotherhood of the Demon Wind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T09:14:01-08:00","id":793610,"title":"","content":"I'd like to add my voice to the crowd chanting Dreamspeakers.<br /> <br /> I'd alao like to throw in the Orphans of Proteus. They were a Legacy that always captured my interest, but the core book Legacies suffered the problem of the line finding its feet, and the Life-focused ones in particular struggled due to the restrictions on the arcanum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T09:16:48-08:00","id":793612,"title":"","content":"Forge Masters can make really cool non-stereotype Moros Adamantine Arrow Legacy. They even basically are one, as per the write-up in <b>Legacies: The Ancient</b>, where most members are hailing from Arrows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-27-2015, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T09:21:28-08:00","id":793614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=793612#post793612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forge Masters can make really cool non-sterotype Moros Adamantine Arrow Legacy. They even basically are one, as per the write-up in Legacies, where most memebers are hailing from Arrows.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, they really could have. Sadly, the Moros slot is already taken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png