ontent":"Brotherhood of the Demon Wind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2060-cthulusbuttcheeks","name":"CthulusButtCheeks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T09:34:49-08:00","id":793629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=793614#post793614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, they really could have. Sadly, the Moros slot is already taken.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually from what Dave wrote he has an Acanthus and and idea for Mastigos with Moros, Obrimos and Thyrsus open.<br /> <br /> Also like Forge masters as arrows seems natural and cool, while also being notably different from other arrow legacies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T09:36:18-08:00","id":793630,"title":"","content":"Uh, no, Moros are in the corebook. The 11th Question are Moros.<br /> <br /> Forge Masters also kinda rely on the Perfected Materials, which won't be until Signs of Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T09:47:01-08:00","id":793641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=793630#post793630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forge Masters also kinda rely on the Perfected Materials, which won't be until Signs of Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you promise them in<b> Signs of Sorcery</b> then, we will wait for them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T09:47:49-08:00","id":793642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=793630#post793630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> Forge Masters also kinda rely on the Perfected Materials, which won't be until Signs of Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>So does that mean alchemy will make a reappearance in signs of sorcery as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T10:02:46-08:00","id":793650,"title":"","content":"Again I try to correct someone and fail terribly. Well, happens, i guess....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T10:05:11-08:00","id":793653,"title":"","content":"I would say for acanthus (or at least acanthus feel): House of Ariadne.<br /> <br /> If forge master is a no for it dependence on signs of sorcery i would suggest the tamers of fire. Why? Because at the very least they are a template on how design the attaiments for the other tamers until they are release.<br /> <br /> I would suggest bokor, the pefected adepts and the demon wind.<br /> <br /> As a side question would we get in the core a guideline to make our own legacies until the ones we want are release?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T10:08:46-08:00","id":793656,"title":"","content":"For the Mastigos slot, I am torn between <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Clavicularius/Bene Ashmedai and Reality Stalkers. The former tap into some very powerful themes and the 2nd Edition mechanics could really give them a chance to shine. The latter provide not only a less standard (not Mind based) view on the Path, but also an obvious seedy underside to the Mysterium. Their actions comprise everything from, on one end - spying, smuggling and theft, on the other - pocket dimensions and Abyssal threats. Also, the Ladder slot is already taken.<br /> <br /> For Thyrsus/Free Council - Dreamspeakers. The Legacy was written up before Astral Realms was released. Writing them again with new material in mind is a challenging undertaking, but definitely worth the effort. Also, they are a perfect fit for the Order.</span></span><br /> <br /> For Obrimos/Adamantine Arrow - Tamers of Fire. Mostly due to what LokiRavenSpeak said.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=793650#post793650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again I try to correct someone and fail terribly. Well, happens, i guess....</div> </div> </div> </div>It's cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 12-27-2015, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T10:42:34-08:00","id":793673,"title":"","content":"My ST says he'd prefer to see Blank Badges and Katsinam Tsuukya as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T10:56:10-08:00","id":793678,"title":"","content":"I remember reading this Mastigos Legacy years ago, and I recall was surprisingly good, because they went directly against the &quot;typical&quot; take on Mastigos. Tamers of... Void? I don't recall what Order they favoured, but I hope it fits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T11:02:23-08:00","id":793683,"title":"","content":"Tamers of the Cave?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T11:10:50-08:00","id":793688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=793683#post793683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tamers of the Cave?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just checked the wiki and that's right, that's the Legacy I was thinking of. Since they say Order: Any, I think they could fit well with the Adamantine Arrow, as a unique take on conflict (I can imagine a Tamer of the Cave casually putting himself in danger and explaining to his apprentice, using the King's Gambit as a chess metaphor, the value of strategical sacrifice).<br /> <br /> That would allow for another combination of Obrimos/Thyrsus and Free Council/Mysterium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T11:25:48-08:00","id":793694,"title":"","content":"I'm coming out of lurking to weigh in on this subject just because it is so dear to my heart.<br /> <br /> First off, I'm surprised that there's only one vote for the Daksha. Everyone should vote for the Daksha. The Daksha are the best worst mages ever. Vote for the Daksha.<br /> <br /> Secondly, as much as I love the Clavicularii/Bene Ashmedai, including them would kind of limit choices to the other two Paths if you want to also include all the Orders, as you're now stuck with two Silver Ladder Legacies (which is never actually a bad thing).<br /> <br /> Thirdly, and call me crazy for saying this, but why not make totally new Legacies? You can get whatever matchups you want to fit the whole 5 Paths and 5 Orders thing, and you give the readers a totally new treat instead of just a revision (also not actually a bad thing - especially if the Daksha are involved). Another choice could be to detail one/a few of the Legacies that were only mentioned in various books but never fully written up (like the Haruspices and the Hotspur Brigade).<br /> <br /> In the end, though, if I had to make three choices from the existing Legacies, I'd go for the Daksha, the Brotherhood of the Demon Wind, and the Dreamspeakers. Alternatively, I could go with the Whipping Boys (which would now be open to the Arrow as well) and the Sphinxes for the former two instead.<br /> <br /> Daksha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T11:33:29-08:00","id":793696,"title":"","content":"Tamer Legacies should be Order: None or Order: Free Council - they were always on the outskirts of Orders and highly connected to particular Paths. In 2ED they still could be teach to anyone, if new member will have Praxis - but I would still makes them mostly Nameless thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=793694#post793694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, I'm surprised that there's only one vote for the Daksha. Everyone should vote for the Daksha. The Daksha are the best worst mages ever. Vote for the Daksha.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was pointing by <b>DaveB</b> that chosen Legacies should not be Left-Handed. Daksha are (almost) those, so this is why I would rather put <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Eyes of Ain Soph</span></span> or Reality Stalkers for Mysterium in their place.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T11:34:53-08:00","id":793697,"title":"","content":"While they're a great legacy, I think the Daksha would be difficult to do properly. They really need a lot of context to explain and you're simply not going to get that in a corebook entry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T11:37:01-08:00","id":793698,"title":"","content":"The main reason not to make new ones, I assume, is because that entails more work than revising existing legacies, and this is basically a freebie project as a favor to us. It also leaves development space open for legacies in future products.<br /> <br /> What I think would be nice is specifically updating legacies whose attainments aren't clearly modeled on spells. Like the Blank Badges, or the Ascended Adepts, they fall into a kind of conceptual crack between the direct translation of spell to attainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T11:38:04-08:00","id":793699,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=793698#post793698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I think would be nice is specifically updating legacies whose attainments aren't clearly modeled on spells. Like the Blank Badges, or the Ascended Adepts, they fall into a kind of conceptual crack between the direct translation of spell to attainment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, this reasoning I would also nicely vote for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=793697#post793697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They really need a lot of context to explain and you're simply not going to get that in a corebook entry.</div> </div> </div> </div>We talk about corebook inclusion here? I thought <b>DaveB</b> had in mind blog posts with Legacies - like was done with <b>Vampire</b> and Bloodlines for 2ED...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T11:39:03-08:00","id":793700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=793699#post793699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We talk about corebook inclusion here? I thought <b>DaveB</b> had in mind blog posts with Legacies - like was done with Vampire and Bloodlines for 2ED...</div> </div> </div> </div>That is what Dave meant, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T11:45:27-08:00","id":793703,"title":"","content":"Yeah I would like the Daksha and the brotherhood of the demon wind","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T12:01:49-08:00","id":793710,"title":"","content":"WOA!! u gota Daksha!!! hnnn.... i gota have dat Daksha... but i gota have Relati Stokers, hnnnn....!!! teetime always wanna Relati Stokers...!<br /> <br /> I'm so sorry!<br /> <br /> ...no I'm not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T12:01:57-08:00","id":793711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We talk about corebook inclusion here? I thought <b>DaveB</b> had in mind blog posts with Legacies - like was done with <b>Vampire</b> and Bloodlines for 2ED... </div> </div> </div>Ah, I misunderstood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T12:12:57-08:00","id":793720,"title":"","content":"Really where are the bloodlines I can't find them on the homepage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T12:17:57-08:00","id":793722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=793720#post793720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really where are the bloodlines I can't find them on the homepage.</div> </div> </div> </div>You need to dig through the previous articles under Requiem. The specific bloodline writeups aren't labelled as such, their titles merely reference the name of the particular bloodline. Look for 'The Shadow and the Asp' for the Khaibit for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T12:35:27-08:00","id":793727,"title":"","content":"Mastigos: Bene Ashmedai/Clavicularius please, their dealings with Vice and goetic entities are a great fit for a mastigos Legacy. This opens up the possibility to explore a Legacy that deals with a class of ephemeral beings.<br /> Even if they represent the Silver Ladder, other Legacies may fill in for two other Orders (such as the 11th Question already did).<br /> <br /> Obrimos: Eyes of Ain Soph are my favorite Obrimos legacy due to their Qabalah trappings. They are a perfect example of Obsession-ridden Mystagogues.<br /> <br /> Thyrsus: Orphans of Proteus are somewhat iconic, imho, so my vote goes to them. I'd also make a case for making the Lords of the Innanimate a Free Council Legacy (or at least share it with the SL), in the spirit of &quot;all things humanity make have great spirits inside of them&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T12:40:38-08:00","id":793733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yuukale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=793727#post793727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also make a case for making the Lords of the Innanimate a Free Council Legacy (or at least share it with the SL), in the spirit of &quot;all things humanity make have great spirits inside of them&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really <i>caring</i> about the tools you use for your particular Sleeper craft seems like quite a Free Council thing to me, too.<br /> <br /> (I may or may not have some notes for a Freak Lord of the Inanimate biker going by &quot;Tool-Using Mammal&quot; somewhere. ;-) )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T12:51:44-08:00","id":793740,"title":"","content":"I really want to see the Daksha return in 2e, but treated as an antagonist legacy. Fangs of Mara, Tremere-cursed, Echo Walkers, and some scelestii forms would all be welcome in that treatment.<br /> <br /> For the right handed side:<br /> Dreamspeakers (Thyrsus) or Proteans<br /> Clavicularius (Mastigos) or Subtle Ones<br /> Uncrowned Kings (Moros) or Bokor<br /> Thrice-Great (Obrimos) or Stewards of the Celestial Orrery seem like good iconic choices.<br /> Walkers in the Mist (Accanthus)<br /> <br /> Blank Badges (N/A, really)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 12-28-2015, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T12:52:34-08:00","id":793741,"title":"","content":"Daksha, Thrice-Great (I propose change their name to greek Trimegistos, it sound more mystical) and Dreamspeakers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T13:08:54-08:00","id":793753,"title":"","content":"Not a regular Mage player, but I do buy the occasional pdf, have the 1e corebook in hardcover, and do love me some Mage in my Vampire and mortal games. The legacies that have peaked my interest the most (aside from the Left-Handed ones) are the <b>Thrice-Great</b> (and second that their name should be changed to <i>Trismegistoi</i>, if used for plural, or <i>Trismegistos</i>), the <b>Clavicularius</b>, and either the <b>Daksha</b> or the <b>Dreamspeakers </b>(or both, preferably).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T13:10:09-08:00","id":793755,"title":"","content":"I agree with the Thrice-Great. I really liked those guys, and it'd be interesting to see more info on the planetary spirits it introduced in passing which were never brought up again (least as far as I know).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (I propose change their name to greek Trimegistos, it sound more mystical) </div> </div> </div>I don't really see that. The three motif makes it automatically sound like something mystical whilst also conveying a pretty good impression of the way the legacy views itself. Trimegistos is only mystical if you know who it refers to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T13:14:51-08:00","id":793758,"title":"","content":"Rules of propositions are simple - <b>3 Legacies max, One Legacy per </b><b>Path and One per Order, no Left Hand</b>. Because of below...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=793753#post793753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The legacies that have peaked my interest the most (aside from the Left-Handed ones) are the <b>Thrice-Great</b> (and second that their name should be changed to <i>Trismegistoi</i>, if used for plural, or <i>Trismegistos</i>), the <b>Clavicularius</b>,.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can agree with Thrice-Great name change, but going with both T-G and Clavicularius would mean next two Silver Ladder groups chosen. With Sisterhood of the Bleesed the <b>DaveB</b> made it would make it almost Silver Ladder only project... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I love some parts of Ladder philosophy, but this project should be about <i>ALL Orders</i>, showing the power in them just after the new corebook release, not only Silver Ladders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=793755#post793755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really see that. The three motif makes it automatically sound like something mystical whilst also conveying a pretty good impression of the way the legacy views itself. Trimegistos is only mystical if you know who it refers to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clavicularius is also very not easy to understand as name, but it's in the Latin version as groups name. Not to mentioned Bene Ashmeda, who's to this day I do not know how to pronounce...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-27-2015, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T14:21:11-08:00","id":793777,"title":"","content":"&quot;Ben - Eh - Ash - May - Die&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T14:31:02-08:00","id":793779,"title":"","content":"As I love the idea that you use your magic to change your body I vote for:<br /> Daksha - I love the legacy.<br /> Transhuman engineers - awesome concept, failed execution.<br /> Perfected adept - Magic is not an excuse to neglect your body, I would love to add how exploring the human body and its capabilties give supernal knowledge.<br /> <br /> The quiescent - Intresting legacy.<br /> <br /> Timori - A banisher legacy struck me as out of place, maybe it could be reworked?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7463-toine","name":"Toine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7463_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T14:36:19-08:00","id":793781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=793777#post793777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Ben - Eh - Ash - May - Die&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It should be more like &quot;meh - dah&quot; than &quot;may - die.&quot;<br /> <br /> In an attempt to provide more productive commentary I argue against Daksha being in, in favor of... I don't know, Perfected Adepts, because hermaphroditic ubermenschen don't exactly strike me as the best introductory choice. I'd also like to see Clavicularius for Mastigos and uh. I don't know. Something Free Council for Thyrsus. How about Dreamspeakers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":77,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","user":"kongurous","date":". 12-27-2015, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T14:37:00-08:00","id":793783,"title":"","content":"Timori are disqualified by being left handed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T14:42:26-08:00","id":793787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Clavicularius is also very not easy to understand as name, but it's in the Latin version as groups name. Not to mentioned Bene Ashmeda, who's to this day I do not know how to pronounce... </div> </div> </div>I agree. That's why I'd leave the Thrice-Great alone. Titles don't have much weight if few people know what they mean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T14:43:19-08:00","id":793789,"title":"","content":"I vote:<br /> Obrimos: Perfected Adepts.<br /> Mastigos: Clavicularius<br /> Thyrsus: Dreamspeakers.<br /> <br /> Perfected Adepts and Clavicularius are iconic, and rather fundamental Legacies as I see them. The Dreamspeakers win points for being one of the only legacies to touch upon the Free Council's &quot;nameless alliance&quot; heritage, which is being further emphasized in 2e. So it makes sense for them to step up for the Free Council slot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/103-gsd","name":"GSD","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T16:07:27-08:00","id":793821,"title":"","content":"So, two setups I'm considering that fits the mold we're looking for:<br /> Obrimos/Arrow - Perfected Adept<br /> Thyrsus/Council - Dreamspeakers<br /> Mastigos/Mysterium - The Sphinx<br /> <br /> Of course, I'd much rather prefer a different legacy than the Sphinx, but this is the one that comes to, given their puzzle box obsession, it could be made to fit (whereas the Clavicularius would need a mild rewrite, well within DaveB's power should he choose to expand them, which wouldn't be a bad thing!)<br /> <br /> The other goes a slightly different route, but runs into a different problem:<br /> <br /> Obrimos/Mysterium - Daksha<br /> Thyrsus/Council - Dreamspeakers<br /> Mastigos/Arrow - Brotherhood of the Demon Wind<br /> <br /> Brotherhood of the Demon Wind is a fairly unknown legacy, and not really gotten a lot of attention. Plus while most people think the Obrimos as fighters and the Mastigos as schemers, this sort of puts everything upside down. However it doesn't strike me as Iconic like the previous setup.<br /> <br /> Ideally, I'd go with GSD's suggestion of Perfected Adept, Dreamspeakers and Clavicularius, but again, we gotta include all the orders. I'd prefer the former over the second.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/650-dtemplar5","name":"DTemplar5","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar650_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T16:33:36-08:00","id":793835,"title":"","content":"So for me, the three that I would pick are:<br /> Thyrsus - Dreamspeakers<br /> Obrimos - Perfected Adepts<br /> Mastigos - Clavicularius<br /> <br /> Few reasons for this.<br /> <br /> I think the Dreamspeakers are themselves just a great Legacy to illustrate the Free Council not as technomancers or something similar. They emphasize the Libertine ideal of drawing on human belief systems and working outside of the Diamond and Seer frameworks. It's a solid obvious Thyrsus Legacy and also a good &quot;break stereotypes&quot; Free Council one.<br /> <br /> I like Perfected Adepts since I think the one group that seems to have a dirth of Legacies in general seems to be the Arrows overall. It's also nice since it shows a bit of how the themes of a Path outgrow into other Arcana in general. And if there's going to be an Arrow-specific one, I'd greatly rather have the about physical self cultivation than what in effect is a bit too on the nose modern samurai wankery thing.<br /> <br /> Clavicularius just seem neat, a very iconic bit of magical thematics to utilize and stand out nicely I think as a result. I think this is the one that I would say is most negotiable on my tastes though. <br /> <br /> If there's a real need for a Mysterium/Mastigos one, the Sphinx is neat for being very Mystegogue and metamagic-based in its goals. But also just some Tamers of the Cave might not be bad either.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T16:36:20-08:00","id":793837,"title":"","content":"Id go for:<br /> <br /> Mastigos: Sphinx, Bene Ashmedai/Clavicularius, Reality Stalkers<br /> Obrimos: Perfected Adept, Eyes of Ain Soph, or Ascended Adept<br /> Thyrsus<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />reamspeakers, Orphan of Proteus, Neocologists","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T16:58:29-08:00","id":793847,"title":"","content":"I want to see the Whipping Boys... I like those...<br /> But since it's unlikely that they will get chosen as the Obrimos example, I'll say that I'd be really happy with either of the Adepts, preferably the Ascended.<br /> Although their Astral-focus might collide a bit with the Dreamspeakers...<br /> <br /> The Brotherhood of the Demon wind is nice. It's a &quot;cool&quot; group, and it'd be nice to get some combat-focused group. Just as we got the Khabiti for Vampire.<br /> <br /> I agree with the Dreamspeakers for Thyrsus. It is shamanism on a whole different level, plus the fact that Thyrsus have Mind as Inferior has been a bit of a problem for them in my campaigns. Having a Mind-focused Legacy would be really nice.<br /> But if their reliance on the Astral is a problem, perhaps the Keepers of the Covenant would fit? They are an enhancement of the Thyrsus archetype, after all.<br /> <br /> For Acanthus I'd like the Daoine. Going all-out on the Fate part.<br /> <br /> Finally, attached to no specific path, I'd like to see an update of the Scions of God. I like their ideas of being kinda-sorta a spirit. But their fluff needs serious fixing, as it is extremely unfocused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T17:10:07-08:00","id":793854,"title":"","content":"One of the problems I have with most of the Arrow legacies, and some legacies in particular...how do they obsess over and explore Mysteries in general? That really needs reworking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T17:38:35-08:00","id":793859,"title":"","content":"Nthing the requests for Clavicularius and Dreamspeakers, since those are/could be very important to upcoming games I hope to be in or run.<br /> <br /> For Obrimos, I think redoing the Choir of the Hashallim would be neat since it would integrate the new Supernal Entities rules, although Thrice Great would also be sweet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 12-27-2015, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T17:55:31-08:00","id":793865,"title":"","content":"Who were those crazy fucks who worshiped the angels of the Realm of Aether?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T19:31:03-08:00","id":793894,"title":"","content":"I must put in my bid for the Sphinxes. A Mastigos I played once drove his peers absolutely bonky with that legacy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6770-midgardener","name":"Midgardener","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6770_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T22:35:23-08:00","id":793967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=793865#post793865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who were those crazy fucks who worshiped the angels of the Realm of Aether?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you probably mean the Echo Walkers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T23:10:30-08:00","id":793977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=793967#post793967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you probably mean the Echo Walkers.</div> </div> </div> </div>But <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Choir of Hashmallim also work with description of &quot;</span></span>crazy fucks who worshiped the angels of the Realm of Aether&quot; - we have one in our London game from Guardians, and it fit's the specification. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Still, Choir have only Obsession on fighting the Abyss using their Summoned Agnels - Echo Walkers are those that take souls to watch Aether all the time.<br /> <br /> Mentioning it - <b>Does not Echo Walkers reason for the existence is removed in 2ED?</b> When <b>every</b> mage has ability to Focus his Mage SIght and see Supernal Realm around you for cost of only Mana - Why you would steal peoples souls for it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-28-2015, 02:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T23:14:00-08:00","id":793980,"title":"","content":"Free Council: Blank Badges","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T23:29:51-08:00","id":793992,"title":"","content":"Another Dreamspeakers vote","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T01:54:36-08:00","id":794042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=793977#post793977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Choir of Hashmallim also work with description of &quot;</span></span>crazy fucks who worshiped the angels of the Realm of Aether&quot; - we have one in our London game from Guardians, and it fit's the specification. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Still, Choir have only Obsession on fighting the Abyss using their Summoned Agnels - Echo Walkers are those that take souls to watch Aether all the time.<br /> <br /> Mentioning it - <b>Does not Echo Walkers reason for the existence is removed in 2ED?</b> When <b>every</b> mage has ability to Focus his Mage SIght and see Supernal Realm around you for cost of only Mana - Why you would steal peoples souls for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>A very valid point, in fact. Part of why they could help explain the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T02:20:03-08:00","id":794052,"title":"","content":"For the mastigos / mysterium I vote for the reality stalkers. They're my favourite legacy and a legacy with abyssal ties like the reality stalkers often have would make for a very interesting group to include in the 2nd edition mage setting. Otherwise the celestial masters for the moros / free council / silver ladder are a fantastic legacy, a group of astronomers who transform energy into matter and back again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T06:57:18-08:00","id":794143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=793758#post793758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rules of propositions are simple - <b>3 Legacies max, One Legacy per </b><b>Path and One per Order, no Left Hand</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know I was probably breaking the rules for voting, just felt like I had to pick the Legacies closer to <i>personal experience</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T07:09:29-08:00","id":794150,"title":"","content":"Throwing in my vote behind Clavicarius/Bene Ashmodai for the Mastogos legacy(ies) - my favorite existing legacies, and a very interesting aspect of the Legacy system that I want examined more closely. Plus they very well exemplify big elements of their parent Path (seeking self mastery) and Order (allowing magic other orders find hubristic).<br /> <br /> Tamers of Fire or Perfected Adepts would both be natural choices for Obrimos/Arrow<br /> <br /> I'd say the Sodality of Tor for Thyrsis - I don't think they had an official parent Order in 1e, but they make perfect sense as a 2e Libertine legacy.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1200-doink","name":"Doink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T07:20:15-08:00","id":794161,"title":"","content":"I would also vote for the Choir of Hashmallim for Obrimos. The interaction between a legacy and Supernal is bound to be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T07:39:30-08:00","id":794179,"title":"","content":"I am one of those that love the Goetic related legacies for Mastigos. So +1 for Clavicularius and Bene Ashmedai.<br /> <br /> I also enjoy The Dreamspeakers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8022-kinok0","name":"kinok0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T07:42:47-08:00","id":794180,"title":"","content":"I'm voting Dreamspeakers for Thrysus, Free Council.<br /> <br /> Though if you're not averse to a more significant retcon, I'd <i>prefer</i> Roses of Eden, which I think should be Thrysus with Fate instead of Acanthus with Life. That might hew too closely to your &quot;no Left-Handed&quot; prohibition, though interpreting both Legacies would be an interesting challenge, and provide STs with neat story tools (which Legacy were you inducted to, again...?).<br /> <br /> Either would be an interesting example of a nearly-Nameless Order (one that predates the Diamond, one that postdates) that hangs out in the Free Council.<br /> <br /> (I also like the Thrice-Great.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 12-28-2015, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T08:16:43-08:00","id":794195,"title":"","content":"I would love to see Clavicularius/Bene Ashmedai in the core as an example of divergent legacies to get players' and storytellers creative juices flowing as well as an excellent choice for the Mastigos legacy.<br /> <br /> Would like to throw an extra voice for Dreamspeakers as Thyrsus / Free Council legacy, as it allows to flesh out Astral a bit more as well as shed more light on Free Counsil predecessors in Nameless orders and their alternative worldviews<br /> <br /> While I personally prefer Eyes of Ain Soth and would love to see them updated, I think the core would be best served by Tamers of Fire as an Obrimos legacy.<br /> <br /> PS Would also really like to see Parliament of the Needle made official or at the very least converted to 2e =)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10044-arcanephysics","user":"ArcanePhysics","date":". 12-28-2015, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10044-arcanephysics","name":"ArcanePhysics","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T08:43:20-08:00","id":794204,"title":"","content":"I'll throw in for the Clavicularius/Bene Ashmedai as well. I would also love to see the Forge Masters and the Wraiths of Epochs updated","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/898-kurasu","name":"kurasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar898_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T09:05:54-08:00","id":794212,"title":"","content":"Sphinxes, please! I'd very much like to see how the various parts of that legacy (reading Fate &amp; connections, linguistics, and coding) all come together in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/518-alieron","name":"Alieron","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T10:11:09-08:00","id":794243,"title":"","content":"I was going to vote multiple times for The Sodality of Thor, but then i saw you already had an Acanthus in your list. Then i went straight for the Scions of God, but they were a Silver Ladder Legacy. Dammit!<br /> <br /> So... i'll vote for Perfected Adepts, or the Thrice Great. And Dreamspeakers, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":1349,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","user":"Phersus","date":".  Forgetting about the Thrive Great was just silly of me. 12-28-2015, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T10:27:28-08:00","id":794259,"title":"","content":"I vote for the Daksha! I don't think they're quite left-handed. They're more... ambidextrous. :P<br /> <br /> I like the Perfected Adepts. They feel kinda Fight Club. And I can pervert the write-up for my drug-abusing Imperfect Adepts! <br /> <br /> And the Bokor! But... Moros is already taken. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":196,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","user":"Max Deltree","date":". 12-28-2015, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T11:23:30-08:00","id":794286,"title":"","content":"The Quiescent and Daksha are at the top of my list, though the Brotherhood of the Demon Wind and any of the Seer legacies are close behind.<br /> <br /> I'd love to see updates to the Echo Walkers and Secret Order of the Gate once you do delve into the Left-Handed stuff, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T13:30:04-08:00","id":794361,"title":"","content":"The Nameless orders should really get the same sort of treatment as sinister stuff got in <i>Left-Handed Path</i>. I think that the Elemental Tamers should be covered in depth in such a book rather than just in a list o' legacies format. (I liked those, but they needed more to them)<br /> <br /> At first I thought of that as an argument <i>against</i> using Tamers of Fire as the Obrimos in-core example, but I've changed my mind on that point. Such an appetizer would be quite welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T14:53:00-08:00","id":794400,"title":"","content":"Oh, I'd also like to see an item-crafting centric legacy, but feel that it should be an Obrimos Matter-primary Prime-secondary rather than the existing Power Smiths (I think that's what they are). The whole Legacy and the idea of crafting items for power oozes Obrimos much more than Moros, imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T14:55:35-08:00","id":794402,"title":"","content":"Delete....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2205,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2205-abaddon","user":"Abaddon","date":". 12-28-2015, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2205-abaddon","name":"Abaddon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T15:05:19-08:00","id":794409,"title":"","content":"I vote for the Elemental Tamers, but if you don't mind splitting them up I would vote for the Tamers of Winds in particular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T15:38:53-08:00","id":794425,"title":"","content":"I like better versions of the Threndolgists and the other technology based legacy. Obrimos need something not so religious, crafting, or supernal focused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 12-28-2015, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T17:53:57-08:00","id":794502,"title":"","content":"Dreamspeakers and Choir of Hashmallim would be awesome ways to really delve into the newly streamlined astral and supernal rules, respectively. Considering that the Supernal and its entities are now around you and visible, it should make for an interesting change in the fluff. Plus, adding two extra attainments (1 and 5 Dot) should make both of those legacies really interesting (well, since summoning is its own attainment, the Choir might get a new 3 dot power too).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T21:32:49-08:00","id":794597,"title":"","content":"I so need the Transhuman Engineers as the Obrimos Path/Free Council Order to get a second edition makeover. Besides that you already got the Tremere slated so I'm a happy camper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Things need not have happened to be true. Tales and dreams are the shadow truths that will endure when mere facts are dust and ashes, and forgot.&quot; Sandman (Neil Gaiman)","edited":{"userid":733,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/733-troller","user":"Troller","date":". 12-29-2015, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/733-troller","name":"Troller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T02:20:33-08:00","id":794699,"title":"","content":"For many of the reasons mentioned by others previously (that I won't elaborate upon bc it's 2 am and going to bed is probably way more reasonable then spending the next half hour writing half coherently about wizards.) I'm voting Clav/Bene, Dreamspeakers, and Perfected Adept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1835-eltommo","name":"eltommo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1835_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T07:15:26-08:00","id":794808,"title":"","content":"Thyrsus: Imagineers (FC).<br /> <br /> (Should probably have Mind as their ruling Arcanum, all of their Attainments deal with the Astral).<br /> <br /> Obrimos:Perfected Adept (AA)<br /> <br /> Mastigos: Subtle Ones (GotV)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":6508,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","user":"Tambov","date":". 12-29-2015, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T07:30:12-08:00","id":794815,"title":"","content":"Kinda sad that 11th Question is &quot;the&quot; Moros legacy. I like Questions, no question, but they don't feel very Moros-y or very Guardian-y for me. Always thought that Uncrowned Kings worked perfectly as postercharacters for Moros-Free Council, capturing their themes, synergizing them and crafting them into new quality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T07:35:07-08:00","id":794818,"title":"","content":"Imagineers were poorly designed, in a lot of ways they come off like half-assed Dreamspeakers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T08:33:51-08:00","id":794847,"title":"","content":"I know it's very late to come into the conversation and say this, but I feel like it needs to be said: Find a legacies that is Obrimos, Mastigos, or Thyrsus AND could applies to TWO Orders, preferrably Arrows, Mysterium, or Council. Everyone is suggesting their favorite Legacy that only seems to apply to one Order. I only say this because some suggestions like Daksha and other things are hard to apply to more than one Order without a lot of exposition. /rant<br /> <br /> In order to be constructive to this conversation, I would like the second (or third) the Tamers of Fire as an Obrimos Legacy that is for the Arrows and the Free Council.<br /> <br /> Mimir's Voice as a Mastigos Legacy that finds members among the Free Council and the Mysterium.<br /> <br /> Keepers of the Covenant as a Thrysus Legacy that is Silver Ladder and Free Council<br /> <br /> The Blank Badges are too cool not to include. Mastigos and they would be Free Council/Guardians of the Veil. I feel like the Blank Badges concept goes well with the Masques and the Free Council would be so pissed that the GoV stole their thunder to subvert their teachings.<br /> <br /> Or perform another switch up and include the Subtle Ones and make them GoV/Free Council as the two Orders use the Legacies powers to shape society in opposing directions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T10:02:48-08:00","id":794911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=794815#post794815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinda sad that 11th Question is &amp;quot;the&amp;quot; Moros legacy. I like Questions, no question, but they don't feel very Moros-y or very Guardian-y for me. Always thought that Uncrowned Kings worked perfectly as postercharacters for Moros-Free Council, capturing their themes, synergizing them and crafting them into new quality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I...actually have to agree. Dont get me wrong, I love them as a legacy (one of my top 10, for sure). <br /> <br /> But they are described in 1e as being a group that runs contrary to the Guardians on a number of things (they drag into the light while the Guardians hide in the Dark). And their themes never hit me as being as Moros as the Uncrowned Kings or other Moros legacies.<br /> <br /> That said, I think it is a perfect choice to show how much a legacy can stray from their origin Path and Order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T11:01:12-08:00","id":794953,"title":"","content":"I always liked them better when they were Mastigos, that's why I rewrote them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T13:19:52-08:00","id":795040,"title":"","content":"Holmes is more Moros than Mastigos and Holmes is the inspiration. The 11th Question is very reliant on physical cues, and not mind reading. 2e tightens up the themes too, as secrets are burdens that people cling to that prevent them from moving on, something that's a more central concern to the Path now. Digging up hidden things is definitely in theme for Moros; Mastigos is more about breaking boundaries and self mastery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T13:40:22-08:00","id":795052,"title":"","content":"A fair take on it. The way the the original legacy was written though made it seem as if the 11Q sink into the minds of the people they investigate. Matter was a sort of throwaway Optional since it only showed up in the 1st attainment. They can know where they're going and why because they can manipulate their own minds to reflect their target's mind. <br /> <br /> I know there's a merit that does that now, but my rewrite took it further. Mastigos are about breaking boundaries? I envisioned the barrier of individuality being broken as the 11Q learns to affect his target's mind just as he effects his own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T01:23:11-08:00","id":797715,"title":"","content":"Brotherhood of the Demon Wind, Sphinxes, Threnodists, Reality Stalkers/Makers, Liberatores, Subtle Ones, Bearers of the Eternal Voice...basically anything BUT Claviclarius or Bene Ashmedai for Mastigos. If I were to pick one, it would be the Brotherhood.<br /> <br /> The Walkers in the Mist or House of Ariadne seems pretty good for Acanthus. Thrice great and perfected Adepts fit Obrimos well. As toThyrsus, well, the dreamspeakers seem interesting.<br /> <br /> That would be my two cents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T08:58:44-08:00","id":798280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=793758#post793758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Clavicularius is also very not easy to understand as name, but it's in the Latin version as groups name. Not to mentioned Bene Ashmeda, who's to this day I do not know how to pronounce...</div> </div> </div> </div>Clavicularius comes from the Latin name of &quot;The Solomon Key&quot; which is Clavicula Salomonis. I suspect the Ashmedai part of Bene Ashmedai to be the Zoroastrian demon of Wrath &quot;Aeshma&quot; who supposedly gave its name to Asmodeus, one of the goetic demon (also appears in other sources) , whose name seems to come from &quot;Aeshma Daeva&quot; (= Wrath of God). Since Asomdai, and several other names this archetype received, is pretty famous through religious and occult/esoteric literature IRL and is mentioned from Zoroastrianism to Judaism and reappear in western middle age, I would assume it was the inspiration. Not to mention Ash May Die, haha","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8022-kinok0","name":"kinok0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T02:03:30-08:00","id":799184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kinok0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=798280#post798280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Clavicularius comes from the Latin name of &quot;The Solomon Key&quot; which is Clavicula Salomonis. I suspect the Ashmedai part of Bene Ashmedai to be the Zoroastrian demon of Wrath &quot;Aeshma&quot; who supposedly gave its name to Asmodeus, one of the goetic demon (also appears in other sources) , whose name seems to come from &quot;Aeshma Daeva&quot; (= Wrath of God). Since Asomdai, and several other names this archetype received, is pretty famous through religious and occult/esoteric literature IRL and is mentioned from Zoroastrianism to Judaism and reappear in western middle age, I would assume it was the inspiration. Not to mention Ash May Die, haha</div> </div> </div> </div>And &quot;Bene&quot; is &quot;sons of&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T04:10:52-08:00","id":799477,"title":"","content":"That mention of Zoroastrianism reminded me. To the Strongest introduced the Clavicularius as having originally been a Zoroastrian Legacy (or at least it's very similiar). I'd be interested to know if that gets taken up or if the rewrite just handwaves it as a parrallel development.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T19:23:11-08:00","id":800043,"title":"","content":"My votes are as follows:<br /> <br /> Mastigos/Arrow: Brotherhood of the Demon Wind<br /> Thyrsus: Chrysalides<br /> Obrimos: Whipping Boys","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition","name":"EmanantVolition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T15:49:36-08:00","id":800779,"title":"","content":"What do the Quiescent look like now that vulgar magic isn't a thing in 2e?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T17:11:15-08:00","id":800817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=800779#post800779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do the Quiescent look like now that vulgar magic isn't a thing in 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Even more awesome.<br /> <br /> Now, seriously, they might still try to abstain from invoking paradoxes and still on the run from the rogue founders. The Quiescent are one of my favorite Legacies (top 5).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T20:06:13-08:00","id":800898,"title":"","content":"Brotherhood of the Demon Wind are one of my favorite Legacies, as are the Reality Stalkers. Above all, I love the House of Ariadne. Even if it was mostly flavor, it was good flavor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10758-uilos","name":"Uilos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T06:18:27-08:00","id":801322,"title":"","content":"I'd vote for the Reality Stalkers because they are Mastigos and they can fit Mysterium, Free Council, Arrows, Guardians, and Seers of the Throne as far as Orders willing to harbor members to apprentice. Their beliefs don't really clash with any of those Orders. The utility of their attainments makes the Legacy useful for spies, stalkers, explorers, intelligence officers, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T07:09:40-08:00","id":801367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=793977#post793977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Mentioning it - <b>Does not Echo Walkers reason for the existence is removed in 2ED?</b> When <b>every</b> mage has ability to Focus his Mage SIght and see Supernal Realm around you for cost of only Mana - Why you would steal peoples souls for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Echo Walkers aren't about seeing the Supernal Realms; they're about seeing the weird angelic proto-humans that are underneath the regular human soul, so they can turn themselves into it with Life magic.<br /> <br /> They didn't even actually steal souls, just kind of peel them up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T14:54:59-08:00","id":801611,"title":"","content":"In line with this thread... does anyone know if there are plans or info on the Uncrowned Kings this time around? I ask because they blew me away and convinced me I wanted to see more of Awakening when I first read about them. They just hit a thematic space I've quite liked precisely on the head, and I would love to know if there are plans to lay them out again. Though they seem pretty easy to adjust to 2e from the spoilers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3547-sonofsilkandstone","name":"SonOfSilkAndStone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T15:24:37-08:00","id":801629,"title":"","content":"The main thing I'm interested in with 2e Uncrowned Kings is how things like that permanent mental shield work - I suspect it may be &quot;if you could get the effect to scene-long reasonably sensibly it can be permanent instead&quot; or something like that in the Attainment rules, but how it works (or if they just make there not be permanent attainments) I'd like to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T15:25:45-08:00","id":801631,"title":"","content":"The main thing would be to bring them under regular Primary/Optional arcana rules since they're spread out a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T15:55:58-08:00","id":801648,"title":"","content":"Mastigos/Mysterium: Sphinxes, because they're such a great concept and I'm interested to see how the Sphinx-O-Vision would be handled in 2E.<br /> Obrimos/Arrow: Perfected Adepts, because they're the epitome of the AA stereotype, which means they fill a common conceptual space, and because they feel like they need some mechanical re-working<br /> Thyrsus/Free Council: Dreamspeakers, because the base Attainment is neat, and as mentioned above they help flesh out the Astral and the FC's Nameless history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4855-eggs-maledict","name":"Eggs Maledict","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T17:11:05-08:00","id":801682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=801367#post801367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Echo Walkers aren't about seeing the Supernal Realms; they're about seeing the weird angelic proto-humans that are underneath the regular human soul, so they can turn themselves into it with Life magic.<br /> <br /> They didn't even actually steal souls, just kind of peel them up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Potayto, potahto - When Obrimos can see literal Angels all the time, they do not need to peel into human soul to see &quot;angelic proto-humans&quot; - they just can see literal Angels of Beauty ( remember that Supernal Beings will have different themes to each one of them ).<br /> <br /> I'm also interested in Echo Walkers as this new difference also makes them interesting as other, non-Obrimos members could lean they Legacy by making good Praxis. If we can make it really worthwhile for Obrimos as Mage Sight modification, maybe other Paths will have their own basis in this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-05-2016, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T17:14:48-08:00","id":801683,"title":"","content":"I... disagree that being able to see Angels of the Aether makes seeing the angelic beings humanity descended from irrelevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T03:58:13-08:00","id":801924,"title":"","content":"All Paths get to see something incredible beneath the Sight. That doesn't stop them from having other interests. Also, Echo Walkers don't just want to see Angels - they want to BE Angels (or something similar). Their way of accomplishing that is dislodging a human soul in search of a missing link. Delving into the Supernal doesn't give them that. However, being able to converse with actual Angels in the 2nd Edition changes things and likely puts an interesting spin on their behaviour.<br /> <br /> At this point I'm not sure if it was in the original write-up, but members of other Paths could have the exact same goal, only with aesthetics changed to match. Instead of targeting a praying human to see an proto-Angel, they target someone during more primal behaviour to see a proto-Beast, and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T06:16:31-08:00","id":802048,"title":"","content":"I\u00b4d definitly want less Legacies. There are way to many. To use them all with ease. <br /> I\u00b4d also want rules for changeing legacies and to in corporate key legacies more to some of the orders.Orders have secrets - and imho these are also legacies. <br /> <br /> Abyssal legacies (not necessesarily &quot;left-handed&quot; ones) Make them additional to a pre-existing - make them easy to attain. Cheap Power = Tainted Power. <br /> <br /> I liked:<br /> The subtle ones. <br /> Hollow ones<br /> Uncrowned kings<br /> These vice-demon peacock legacy (forgot the name) of the silver ladder<br /> The Tremere - &quot;easy immortality&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T06:29:51-08:00","id":802054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maekkel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=802048#post802048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u00b4d definitly want less Legacies. There are way to many. To use them all with ease.<br /> I\u00b4d also want rules for changeing legacies and to in corporate key legacies more to some of the orders.Orders have secrets - and imho these are also legacies.<br /> <br /> Abyssal legacies (not necessesarily &quot;left-handed&quot; ones) Make them additional to a pre-existing - make them easy to attain. Cheap Power = Tainted Power.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's not asking for opinions on the general legacy rules. It's which five legacies would you like to see converted to 2e?<br /> <br /> Also, how exactly do you want them to reduce the number of legacies? Are you saying they need to be withdrawn from publication?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T07:10:08-08:00","id":802070,"title":"","content":"More Legacies gives you more options. You don't have to include them all in your game - take the ones you think will do something interesting, ignore the rest, allow them to exist offscreen or just say &quot;they're not a thing in my incarnation of the setting.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm intending to write <i>quite a lot</i> of Legacies up once 2e drops, because it's fun and I keep having ideas that I think will work - but if I do run a game I won't try and include all my ideas or all the canon ones, just anything that I think will add something fun or interesting to the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T07:21:13-08:00","id":802083,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there's no good reason for less legacies and with the tools for making your own as well you're never going to get less of them.<br /> <br /> I also don't see a reason for rules to change legacies. I've only seen the need for that to happen in one game and it just got hand waved as having been in the preferred legacy all along. Though it could still be good fun to play with the consequences of poor decision making.<br /> <br /> Not sure what you mean by making Abyssal legacies easy to attain. They're not any harder to come by than regular legacies? You want them to be easier than that and throw consistent rules out the window?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T11:20:29-08:00","id":802229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maekkel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=802048#post802048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u00b4d definitly want less Legacies. There are way to many. To use them all with ease.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Wherever did you get the idea that you need to use all published Legacies?<br /> <br /> Not only do not all of them need to show up in your game (as not every Legacy is going to have members in every location a game could take place in), not every Legacy needs to even <i>exist</i> in your setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T14:57:30-08:00","id":806490,"title":"","content":"For Mastigos/Mysterium, I'd definitely like to see the Sphinxes. I love the Sphinxes!<br /> For Obrimos, I wouldn't mind either a write-up for the Ascended Adepts or the Daksha.<br /> For Thyrsus, perhaps the Imagineers, from Free Council.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1494-deranged-goblin","name":"Deranged Goblin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T23:20:16-08:00","id":806799,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see the Thrice-Great come back; they're Obrimos/Silver Ladder, so they fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T11:50:09-08:00","id":809756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=793531#post793531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, right! Also - no Left Handed ones. These are meant to be playable. And I'm already doing the Tremere in the <i>other</i> early thing, which will be a mechanics update for Left Hand Path.<br /> <br /> I'm edging toward doing the Claviclarius/Bene Ashmedai as an example of a Legacy that split, because 2e's Legacy mechanics are better able to model such things than 1e was, and I'm missing a Mastigos one anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div> I really like that idea, plus it like getting two for the price of one.<br /> <br /> But if they're a split legacy it could be interesting to put give them different Order Clav in the Silver Ladder and Bene Ashmedai in say the Free Council, it emphasises the split.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 01-15-2016, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T07:29:35-08:00","id":810219,"title":"","content":"I'd love me some Choir of The Hashmallim, a Legay of Obrimos dedicated to fighting the Abyss in the name of God.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, the Eyes of Ain Soph would be great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T10:00:36-08:00","id":810270,"title":"","content":"The Subtle Ones would be really cool, I love the idea of Mages who are even more invisible than usual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T11:32:55-08:00","id":810305,"title":"","content":"A vote for the Pygmalian Society, please. Loved those guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T05:35:48-08:00","id":811710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=810305#post810305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A vote for the Pygmalian Society, please. Loved those guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that Lucy Sulphate (the Pygmalian Society sample character) is now the primary sample Acanthus Path character, I imagine the Legacy will show up somewhere in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T09:22:58-08:00","id":812669,"title":"","content":"Part of me would like to see Legacies for the Disciple of the World Dragon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T18:58:18-08:00","id":813819,"title":"","content":"On a side note, one thing I'd like to see is how the various Legacies view each other. Now, every Legacy isn't going to have an official view on every other . . . but some of them are clearly going to bump into each other (a lot). For example, the Clavicularius (Clavicularii?), Fallen Pillar, and Fangs of Mara all work extensively with the mentally ill - surely they have stereotypes and opinions of each other? <br /> <br /> So - word count permitting - it might be nice to give each Legacy's general attitude towards the 3-7 Legacies they run into the most (or have the strongest opinion on). Asymmetry would be fine, too - just because Legacy X (say the Transhuman Engineers) have a strong opinion on Legacy Y (the Dreamspeakers, perhaps), that doesn't meant Legacy Y even knows that Legacy X even exists. Helps underscore that many of the Legacies have been around for centuries/millennia, with their own feuds/alliances/etc. <br /> <br /> As for what Legacies should be in the main book (assuming you're still taking suggestions), I definitely support the idea of the Brotherhood of the Demon Wind and the Clavicularius. However, while I'm a big fan of the Elemental Masteries, it might make more sense to hold off, and do all five at the same time. They are all interrelated, after all, and kind of represent the path not taken (to organize mage society, as opposed to the Orders).<br /> <br /> As for the Free Council Legacy . . . I understand why people want the Dreamspeakers. They fits the Free Council themes well, and the Dreamspeakers were a memorable group. I wonder, though, if it would make more sense to use the Roses of Eden or the Blank Badges - two of the anti-Atlantanean Legacies the Order developed to fight the Nameless War/Great Refusal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T19:09:50-08:00","id":813823,"title":"","content":"You're laboring under some misconceptions, none of these are going in the book, and Dave wants a spread of Order/Path representations so Clavicularii and Demon Wind are mutually exclusive because Mastigos.<br /> <br /> I definitely want to see Blank Badges though. They were so badly botched together in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T20:17:40-08:00","id":813869,"title":"","content":"Please give something that isn't focused on gnoetic demons. Give me something that an actual mage might use...investigators, social, combat, curse/luck, espionage. Keep it classic, clear and straightforward. Do the weird non obvious stuff for the new legacy books. We have like 100 published legacies most great ideas but totally implemented in borked ways that suck.<br /> <br /> How about give us 30 legacies that make total sense and are straightforward, obvious and useful in all scenarios. Five per order. Also make sure you make it clear being an Apostate fucks you up in multiple directions hard and never changes.<br /> <br /> For the question at hand I want classic, obvious and straightforward. Obrimos means either Forces or Prime so pick one and do something obvious and easy to see why a player not a GM would actually like it and pick it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 01-21-2016, 11:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T22:03:33-08:00","id":813912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=813869#post813869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please give something that isn't focused on gnoetic demons. Give me something that an actual mage might use...investigators, social, combat, curse/luck, espionage. Keep it classic, clear and straightforward. Do the weird non obvious stuff for the new legacy books. We have like 100 published legacies most great ideas but totally implemented in borked ways that suck.<br /> <br /> How about give us 30 legacies that make total sense and are straightforward, obvious and useful in all scenarios. Five per order. Also make sure you make it clear being an Apostate fucks you up in multiple directions hard and never changes.<br /> <br /> For the question at hand I want classic, obvious and straightforward. Obrimos means either Forces or Prime so pick one and do something obvious and easy to see why a player not a GM would actually like it and pick it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong wrong wrong wrong wrong.<br /> <br /> If you want classic Obrimos... you just play a regular Obrimos. Legacies exist as specific, odd roads for the Awakened soul to walk, as contrast to the generalized Paths they all experience. There are lots of Moros, and every one of them knows Death and Matter, but there are only a handful of Stone Scribes who specialize in the power of True Names.<br /> <br /> A Legacy is not &quot;do the thing you do, but better.&quot; A Legacy is a refinement of the soul and a unique philosophy that ostensibly guides one towards Ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T23:18:19-08:00","id":813937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=813912#post813912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wrong wrong wrong wrong wrong.<br /> <br /> If you want classic Obrimos... you just play a regular Obrimos. Legacies exist as specific, odd roads for the Awakened soul to walk, as contrast to the generalized Paths they all experience. There are lots of Moros, and every one of them knows Death and Matter, but there are only a handful of Stone Scribes who specialize in the power of True Names.<br /> <br /> A Legacy is not &quot;do the thing you do, but better.&quot; A Legacy is a refinement of the soul and a unique philosophy that ostensibly guides one towards Ascension.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bullshit. And only liked by GM's. Fuck that. Again make it easy and then get esoteric. You might disagree but I don't give a damn because what you want isn't what Dave actually asked or what I care about. Pretty simple isn't it?<br /> <br /> Legacies are made for ANY and ALL purposes in 2e. Most should be pretty damn obvious and utilitarian. Sorry if that fucks up your vision of going all Mage the Ascension in Mage the Awakening. Magic is to be used not discussed in a coffee house navel gazing philosophy 101 conversation and there should be obvious advantage to it that isn't stupidly situational. Or what? You figure no mage couldn't figure out how to use the best spells in their path as a praxis and then a legacy attainment? Get real.<br /> <br /> They choose or make a legacy to answer a deep question or focus on a type of magic or possibility they believe in, or curious about but weak in because of path or order or just as a way to protect them and theirs like the Solidarity of Tor among the obvious.<br /> <br /> Or they make legacies focused on finding out or fighting the Abyss in many different ways and at multiple levels and/or focus. Very few legacies are actually focused on Ascension big A. First because few mages actually believe it's a possibility second because most aren't even the business of such a state. Because yes, they don't believe it's a real thing in the first place. Because they are more focused on the very real struggle of ultimate power vs wisdom vs. corruption. Ascension is a fairytale like archmastery for the majority of mages for a variety of reasons. <br /> <br /> They are too busy and focused on answering the smaller questions like immortality or being masters of their home, environment, or other things. Like the House of Adriane or the Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 01-22-2016, 03:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T23:46:17-08:00","id":813948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=813937#post813937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Legacies are made for ANY and ALL purposes in 2e. Most should be pretty damn obvious and utilitarian.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Magic is a tool whose use says nothing about its practitioner&quot; is a view that directly contradicts the established material and has visibly damaged the presentation of Mage as a game built on investigating mysteries rather than knowing everything and having the biggest beatstick. If you have a problem with the idea that legacies are built on philosophies and serve as a potential means of ultimately integrating oneself with magic itself then it's just possible you haven't been paying attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T00:15:05-08:00","id":813954,"title":"","content":"Or maybe you haven't. Don't act like you're smart and I'm stupid. It's pretty offensive. A legacy is about you and your view of the world and maybe just maybe Ascension in some cases. Especially given in 2e all the artificial limits are removed. And you get 1-5 dot spells as legacy attainments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 01-22-2016, 03:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T00:34:13-08:00","id":813960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=813954#post813954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe you haven't. Don't act like you're smart and I'm stupid. It's pretty offensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also offensive: blowing up an incidental mention of Ascension as one of the ultimate endpoints of tying your magical philosophy to your soul into a rant about how This Isn't Classic World Of Darkness, Man.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A legacy is about you and your view of the world and maybe just maybe Ascension in some cases. Especially given in 2e all the artificial limits are removed. And you get 1-5 dot spells as legacy attainments. </div> </div> </div>Yes, thank you, I've read the blog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T00:48:34-08:00","id":813965,"title":"","content":"I have read the same blogs, played the same game, with the same rules. So just get off your high horse because Ascension is not a fact or end goal in Mage the Awakening in either edition. It's a hope, legend, rumor maybe. There's more information about going for archmastery then ascension big A in MtAw and safer in fact.<br /> <br /> And yes, I hate MtAs because they are arguing about the same things we did in 1995 word for word. And I will not stand for mixing the same crap into MtAw. Deal with it. <br /> <br /> It's sad when you find out that you gave away the entire catalog of every version of MtAs because of the fanbase and neverending circular arguments about the very same things argued by me and mine 25 years ago.<br /> <br /> At least with MtAw it's fun and interesting to watch people arrive at conclusions that mostly play well with mine in time. And just pop in from time to time to shake you young bucks up. Much like DnD 5e vs. 0e/1e discussion. Difference is they accept that the latter is a better ruleset no question and totally easy to use when running the former.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 01-22-2016, 04:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T01:05:39-08:00","id":813973,"title":"","content":"But the thing is that Legacies are deeply personal things, they're meant to be strange and esoteric. If you're modyfing your soul to incorporate certain symbols into it, than better those symbols be of actual methaphysical importance. Legacies might seek Ascension or other truths but it's never something utilitarian. I also don't see why a player wouldn't choose to play a Keybearer.<br /> <br /> What I get that is that u want some fairly straightforwards Legacies and that's ok but you're awfully aggresive in your posts. Going by the number of votes in this thread, we're highly likely to get Perfected Adepts who are a very straightforward Legacy. The Eleventh Question from the core book are also quite low on the esoteric. I don't see why we shouldn't get something different alongside those. Also remember that many Legacies have primary arcana different from their Path arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T01:25:42-08:00","id":813988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=813973#post813973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the thing is that Legacies are deeply personal things, they're meant to be strange and esoteric. If you're modyfing your soul to incorporate certain symbols into it, than better those symbols be of actual methaphysical importance. Legacies might seek Ascension or other truths but it's never something utilitarian. I also don't see why a player wouldn't choose to play a Keybearer.<br /> <br /> What I get that is that u want some fairly straightforwards Legacies and that's ok but you're awfully aggresive in your posts. Going by the number of votes in this thread, we're highly likely to get Perfected Adepts who are a very straightforward Legacy. The Eleventh Question from the core book are also quite low on the esoteric. I don't see why we shouldn't get something different alongside those. Also remember that many Legacies have primary arcana different from their Path arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>The straightforward things you guys are voting for are way too straightforward and the other votes are so specialized as to be useless. For example I don't want Fire Tamers as the signature Obrimos legacy that's too obvious. Do a tech based or the Chrior of whatever for example....something useful and meaningful. Why does an Obrimos have to be some kind of bad version of a Shadowrun Adept? <br /> <br /> 11th Question is perfect. It's useful and fits a mages journey about asking questions and finding the answers and fits that path. <br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 01-22-2016, 04:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T01:58:43-08:00","id":813993,"title":"","content":"So it's just that your preferences don't match with other people's preferences ? Getting examples from all around the spektrum would be best for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T02:27:04-08:00","id":814003,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2682_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2682\" data-vbnamecard=\"2682\">Kumiko</a>, you're not going to get 30 legacies, you're going to get 4. You're complaining about something completely subjective when you say a legacy like the claviculari are only interesting to STs. Plus, STs play the most legacies at a time anyways, let them have their fun. Your double standard is annoying, you want legacies that are straightforward and then complain that the legacies in the lead are too straightforward.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2636_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2636\" data-vbnamecard=\"2636\">Menace</a>, legacies can totally be utilitarian, and chosen for utilitarian reasons. That's how Wolsey from BD got into the Bearers of the Eternal Voice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T03:27:01-08:00","id":814022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=814003#post814003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2636_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2636\" data-vbnamecard=\"2636\">Menace</a>, legacies can totally be utilitarian, and chosen for utilitarian reasons. That's how Wolsey from BD got into the Bearers of the Eternal Voice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although they did reject him for apprenticeship <i>because</i> he only wanted their Attainments for utilitarian purposes, and he had to use the lesser-known &quot;study a member's soul stone&quot; method of initiation.<br /> <br /> It's always amusing to see which Legacies people think are &quot;too esoteric to play&quot; or &quot;too boring&quot;. Wolsey's old player has recently joined my ongoing game after moving back into proximity with the rest of us, and, well... He's leaning heavily Perfected Adept.<br /> <br /> Legacies people have actually played in my games - Bearers of the Eternal Voice, House of Ariadne, Uncrowned Kings, Sphinx, two custom Legacies, Children of the Hour, Tamers of Fire, Eleventh Question, and Sisterhood of the Blessed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T04:09:54-08:00","id":814030,"title":"","content":"What I meant is that the guy who <b>starts</b> the legacy doesn't do it with utilitarian purpose. The way I see it, the character doesn't choose or make the attainments, those develop organically according to that persons philosophy or beliefs. He can then pass it on to others, those might have down to earth reasons to join, but I think that a certain amount of understanding of the legacies philosophy is required for joining.<br /> <br /> Dave you meanie, teasing things from The Man Comes Around :&lt; We need a continuation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T05:45:43-08:00","id":814068,"title":"","content":"A great thing about Legacies is that it won't be probably very hard to just create your own Legacy, or create your own take on preexisting one. Mechanically, their design is very clearly communicated and spelled out so you can literally do one on you own without being too much invested into balance and design side of the gamewriting, and fluff wise, it's easy to see a young mage deciding to go &quot;this is how I roll&quot;, while not creating your own Legacy also is a valid and sensible choice.<br /> I'm more sad that picking a Legacy with major arcana that is already major for you is not very optimal. Being refunded up to 2 Arcane Experience over the whole Chronicle, versus having 3rd major arcana and all associated benefits, is well, underwhelming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T05:46:53-08:00","id":814069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=813965#post813965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, I hate MtAs because they are arguing about the same things we did in 1995 word for word. And I will not stand for mixing the same crap into MtAw. Deal with it.<br /> <br /> It's sad when you find out that you gave away the entire catalog of every version of MtAs because of the fanbase and neverending circular arguments about the very same things argued by me and mine 25 years ago.<br /> <br /> At least with MtAw it's fun and interesting to watch people arrive at conclusions that mostly play well with mine in time. <b><u>And just pop in from time to time to shake you young bucks up*1.</u></b> <b><u>Much like DnD 5e vs. 0e/1e discussion. Difference is they accept that the latter is a better ruleset no question and totally easy to use when running the former.*2 </u></b></div> </div> </div> </div>*1what doest that sentence mean? No seriously, what?<br /> <br /> *2 And do we really need a flame war about Ascension vs Awakening? Seriously?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=813937#post813937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again make it easy and then get esoteric.</div> </div> </div> </div>That right there should be the tag line for 2ed mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=813937#post813937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Legacies are made for ANY and ALL purposes in 2e. Most should be pretty damn obvious and utilitarian. Sorry if that fucks up your vision of going all Mage the Ascension in Mage the Awakening. Magic is to be used not discussed in a coffee house navel gazing philosophy 101 conversation and there should be obvious advantage to it that isn't stupidly situational.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage awakening is full of navel gazing, there is even a whole book about it! And wasted a good chunk of Sanctum and sigil on it too!! :P But yes, 1ed like all the other game lines suffered from useless/very situational legacies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=813937#post813937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or what? You figure no mage couldn't figure out how to use the best spells in their path as a praxis and then a legacy attainment? Get real.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, thats true. There will always be players who game the system to get the most powerful powers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=813869#post813869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please give something that isn't focused on gnoetic demons. Give me something that an actual mage might use...investigators, social, combat, curse/luck, espionage. Keep it classic, clear and straightforward. Do the weird non obvious stuff for the new legacy books. We have like 100 published legacies most great ideas but totally implemented in borked ways that suck.</div> </div> </div> </div>i would agree on this with kumiko, while i personally find the goetic demons fascinating. I have never found player took the legacy or use them. They have kinda feel like a blanche card for ST to screw with you for very little gain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=813869#post813869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the question at hand I want classic, obvious and straightforward. Obrimos means either Forces or Prime so pick one and do something obvious and easy to see why a player not a GM would actually like it and pick it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=813988#post813988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The straightforward things you guys are voting for are way too straightforward and the other votes are so specialized as to be useless. For example I don't want Fire Tamers as the signature Obrimos legacy that's too obvious. Do a tech based or the Chrior of whatever for example....something useful and meaningful.</div> </div> </div> </div>So arent you contradicting yourself here? I mean, you said you want an obvious and straightforward obrimos legacy........whats more obvious and straightforward than reflexive, paradox and cost free fireballs? Thats whats mage is all about! FIREBALLS! :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T05:56:23-08:00","id":814075,"title":"","content":"I don't think that you want to put your most powerful spells in attainments, btw. While you get surefire activation and counterspell-no-no, you lose access to Reach and can only assign +2 spell factors at best. They are wonderful for utility spells that you want to cast often, discreetly, and without giving people opening to counter spell them away, but you are stuck with their default state, which doesn't seem very impressivie (at least not for something you would dub as &quot;most powerful spell&quot;). While you might be tempted by Direct-Damage-Fireball Attainment, it's probably better to invest into something like Shifting Sands Attainment, which is a major game changer that reshapes your approach to everyday life immensely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T06:00:30-08:00","id":814078,"title":"","content":"Spammable fireballs beat out regular cast fireballs for reliability.<br /> <br /> Most Mages do have a Rote or Praxis version of their attainments though in case they do need to get more out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T06:45:46-08:00","id":814092,"title":"","content":"@LRS to me it just reads that because Kumiko is old they get to act insufferably entitled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T06:50:40-08:00","id":814096,"title":"","content":"I guess. A lot depends on answer to the very basic question: is &quot;primary factor&quot; of Attainment benefiting from the standard rule of &quot;free factors equal to your Arcana&quot;? Because it's a big difference; Auto-Ball with 1 Potency that can be cranked up to 3 isn't very impressive (in fact, lots of people would just shrug it off with their resistance stat!), while Auto-Ball with guaranteed 6 Potency is a totally different beast. Then again, if Combined Casting still exists and is in similar form to the Combined Casting (that thing that allowed you to cast multiple spells at once for -2 penalty, not &quot;spells combining different arcanas&quot; thing), it might the &quot;best&quot; way to spam direct attack spells.<br /> Also, now I want to see how good would be a MTG Blue legacy based on Counterspelling and saying &quot;nope&quot; to opponent's magical actions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Again, dunno, because it depends on how Counterspell works (my gut says &quot;Clash of Wills&quot;, but how CoW interacts with stuff like Potency and Factors?); AutoCounter with Potency 3 is probably garbage, Potency 6 could be good.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Relevant blog fragment:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Automatic Activation:</b> In most cases, a Legacy Attainment can be activated with an instant action and do not require die rolls. If the Attainment requires spell factors, it automatically confers factors that would impose a penalty up to the mage\u2019s dots in the Attainment\u2019s highest prerequisite Arcanum. If the Attainment would require a measurement of its successes, it automatically scores a number of successes equal to the mage\u2019s dots in the highest prerequisite Arcanum.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">For example, if a fire-summoning Legacy Attainment requires spell factors and requires Forces 3, a Legacy member with Forces 5 harnesses spell factors that would normally impose a -5 penalty to die rolls\u2014though remember that you don\u2019t actually have to roll dice.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T06:59:39-08:00","id":814100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=814022#post814022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although they did reject him for apprenticeship <i>because</i> he only wanted their Attainments for utilitarian purposes, and he had to use the lesser-known &amp;quot;study a member's soul stone&amp;quot; method of initiation.<br /> <br /> It's always amusing to see which Legacies people think are &amp;quot;too esoteric to play&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;too boring&amp;quot;. Wolsey's old player has recently joined my ongoing game after moving back into proximity with the rest of us, and, well... He's leaning heavily Perfected Adept.<br /> <br /> Legacies people have actually played in my games - Bearers of the Eternal Voice, House of Ariadne, Uncrowned Kings, Sphinx, two custom Legacies, Children of the Hour, Tamers of Fire, Eleventh Question, and Sisterhood of the Blessed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave: How many legacies have you already converted for your own use anyways?<br /> <br /> WHW: You should take a look at the Eyes of Ain Soph from the Mysterium book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T07:07:45-08:00","id":814104,"title":"","content":"Considering how important the Astral realms are to <i>all</i> Mages and how iconic Goetia are to Mastigos specifically, the notion that the Clavicularius and Bene Ashmedia wouldn't be useful in a practical sense is utterly bizarre to me. I have a slight preference for Sphinxes, but I still have to admit that the Clavicularius are a better example of a Mastigos Legacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T07:09:33-08:00","id":814105,"title":"","content":"I'll look at them later, but what I have in my head right now is a Prime/Time Legacy (Prime primary, Time secondary) associated with Guardians that focuses on preemptive erasing of magical threats and literally wrist-slapping people who are in middle of casting a spell that &quot;there is no going back from&quot;. Having Shifting Sands as *secondary effect* for 3rd attainment, and Auto-Counter as primary on 2nd sounds like a lot of &quot;nope&quot; potential. Shield of Chronos as supplementary effect would be cool too (so magical criminals can't just walk around you with Time Travel spells). :P<br /> <br /> I always liked idea of Bearers of the Eternal Voice, though due to the fact that permanent memory edits are apparently going to be much, much easier in 2nd edition, they lost a lot of their &quot;oh shit&quot; factor :P. <br /> BTW, for Mastigos Legacy, definitely Brotherhood of Demon Wind. No matter how rude Kumiko is, I have to agree that goetic legacy is not best pick for one of first 5 legacies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T07:14:17-08:00","id":814107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=814100#post814100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dave: How many legacies have you already converted for your own use anyways?</div> </div> </div> </div>So far, just the Sisterhood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T10:02:50-08:00","id":814211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=813954#post813954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe you haven't. Don't act like you're smart and I'm stupid. It's pretty offensive. A legacy is about you and your view of the world and maybe just maybe Ascension in some cases. Especially given in 2e all the artificial limits are removed. And you get 1-5 dot spells as legacy attainments.</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">After receiving multiple reports on this thread and going over it, you're the one repeatedly being offensive. Between the entitlement, insults, dismissive statements towards others, and most importantly edition warring, you are getting a week off. When you come back the attitude had better be improved or more serious sanctions will be levied.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T10:19:17-08:00","id":814224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=814107#post814107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So far, just the Sisterhood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would love to see this. Nothing official, just your take on converting them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T10:32:32-08:00","id":814238,"title":"","content":"Still really want to see some legacies for the Disciples of the World Dragon since they were included at the back end of a splatbook and had some interesting ideas but little substance or life. I'd like to see it become a real faction I guess. <br /> <br /> Also because dragons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T12:22:51-08:00","id":814370,"title":"","content":"Their founder hadn't even started the legacy she was planning yet. That one is really up in the air.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T12:46:31-08:00","id":814393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=814370#post814370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their founder hadn't even started the legacy she was planning yet. That one is really up in the air.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it's now 2e, so perhaps that has changed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T13:09:22-08:00","id":814413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=814224#post814224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would love to see this. Nothing official, just your take on converting them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suggest you reread the OP of this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T13:21:16-08:00","id":814421,"title":"","content":"The Perfected Adepts are my favorites. I'd like to see those (and, indeed, wrote up a 2E version) make it in sometime, because they kick all kinds of ass. Both literally and figuratively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T13:56:36-08:00","id":814437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=814022#post814022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wolsey's old player has recently joined my ongoing game after moving back into proximity with the rest of us, and, well... He's leaning heavily Perfected Adept.</div> </div> </div> </div>You tease!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5958-logocentric","name":"Logocentric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T14:06:00-08:00","id":814443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=814413#post814413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suggest you reread the OP of this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>D'oh. Completely missed that. Thanks Dave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T05:05:22-08:00","id":814789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=814096#post814096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot depends on answer to the very basic question: is &quot;primary factor&quot; of Attainment benefiting from the standard rule of &quot;free factors equal to your Arcana&quot;? Because it's a big difference; Auto-Ball with 1 Potency that can be cranked up to 3 isn't very impressive (in fact, lots of people would just shrug it off with their resistance stat!), while Auto-Ball with guaranteed 6 Potency is a totally different beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the rule applies for Attainments too. They should be based on spells, and from what I've seen, the mechanics are done in such a way that the effects make for more or less equal abilities with different advantages.<br /> <br /> For example, an Exemplar with 5th Attainment (and therefore Mastery of an Arcanum and at least Gnosis 8) would get 5 successes, while someone with Gnosis 8 (or more) and Mastery would roll at least 13 dice, more or less equal to 5 successes too. And that doesn't account for the dice bonuses from Yantras (probably not appliable to an Attainment) and other bonuses you could get. This *already* makes an Attainment weaker than a normal spell.<br /> <br /> As for Reach, from what I think Dave said, it can be used, but only up until you would overreach. So, if you're an Adept, and use an Attainment that's an equivalent to a 3 dot spell, you can apply effects up to two Reach, but not more, so you don't risk Paradox. Makes sense, the Attainments already don't risk Paradox and you shouldn't have your cake and eat it too. Again, the spell and the Attainment are balanced.<br /> <br /> So, because I don't see any balancing issues with spell factors gained by, say, being a Master, I think that free factors are still in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T05:19:07-08:00","id":814791,"title":"","content":"Don't look at number of successes; they are supposed to be irrelevant (other than Exceptional Success). Unless something changed, goal of new magic system was to make number of successes irrelevant by making spell factors &quot;bought&quot; by reducing your dicepool by 2-per-factor. So when looking at 13 dice guy, don't calculate average successes; remove enough dice to either leave him at 3, or at 0 (if she is willing to spend a willpower point on the spell), or at any other number of dice that makes you comfortable when you want 1 success. So the 13 dice dude would probably get up to 5 or 6 factors to spend, depending on usage of willpower.With yantras, you probably can afford another 1 or 2 factors.<br /> I really like how new spellcasting looked when it was teased, because you can see that a lot of math and game design theory was put into it to ensure that it makes sense, is not dependant on swingy nature of dice too much, and rewards making smart DECISIONS.<br /> And provokes you into hubristic ones, because hell, if you have enough time, why not get another 3 factors and reduce yourself to -5 dice and cast the spell multiple times fishing for that 10 :P.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T05:26:53-08:00","id":814794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=814791#post814791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't look at number of successes; they are supposed to be irrelevant (other than Exceptional Success). Unless something changed, goal of new magic system was to make number of successes irrelevant by making spell factors &quot;bought&quot; by reducing your dicepool by 2-per-factor. So when looking at 13 dice guy, don't calculate average successes; remove enough dice to either leave him at 3, or at 0 (if she is willing to spend a willpower point on the spell), or at any other number of dice that makes you comfortable when you want 1 success. So the 13 dice dude would probably get up to 5 or 6 factors to spend, depending on usage of willpower.With yantras, you probably can afford another 1 or 2 factors.<br /> I really like how new spellcasting looked when it was teased, because you can see that a lot of math and game design theory was put into it to ensure that it makes sense, is not dependant on swingy nature of dice too much, and rewards making smart DECISIONS.<br /> And provokes you into hubristic ones, because hell, if you have enough time, why not get another 3 factors and reduce yourself to -5 dice and cast the spell multiple times fishing for that 10 :P.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I used the 5 successes example percisely because of the Exceptional Success, which (or 3 successes for Praxis) is the only relevant number besides a single success. But I still think that the balance is set in such a way that you get additional factors for your Primary factor based on your understanding of an Arcanum.<br /> <br /> EDIT: On a semi-relevant note, Dave mentioned that the mechanics are made in such a way, that mages will probably want to try and get an Exceptional success, rather than just a normal one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 01-23-2016, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T06:01:50-08:00","id":814802,"title":"","content":"yeah, they have something like a whole special list of things you can pick from when you roll super success. I think it's neat, because while most sensible, optimal way to do things is to just do &quot;boring and efficient&quot; transfer-dice-to-factors-and-leave-3, there are nice incentives to go 0 AND BEYOND for more free power, and if you like to gamble, to do the opposite, leaving your spell less powerful as baseline and fishing for crit success; apparently prakses (sorry, was just cleaning my keyboard and vacuum cleaner ate iks key <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) give you ability to achieve super success at 3, instead of 5, which is MASSIVE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T08:20:37-08:00","id":814855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=814238#post814238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still really want to see some legacies for the Disciples of the World Dragon since they were included at the back end of a splatbook and had some interesting ideas but little substance or life. I'd like to see it become a real faction I guess.<br /> <br /> Also because dragons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of that, does transforming yourself into, say, a 10 m long dragon with require a certain anount of Potency on the spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T10:38:49-08:00","id":814913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=814855#post814855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking of that, does transforming yourself into, say, a 10 m long dragon with require a certain anount of Potency on the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand the question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T12:41:09-08:00","id":814974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=814855#post814855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking of that, does transforming yourself into, say, a 10 m long dragon with require a certain anount of Potency on the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, it requires dice penalties for size factors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T12:52:45-08:00","id":814981,"title":"","content":"Probably also a reasonable amount of Potency in 1e or Reach in 2e (I recklessly assume) to get claws <i>and</i> wings <i>and</i> teeth <i>and </i>scales <i>and</i> fire breath. Or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T13:09:22-08:00","id":814989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=814981#post814981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably also a reasonable amount of Potency in 1e or Reach in 2e (I recklessly assume) to get claws <i>and</i> wings <i>and</i> teeth <i>and </i>scales <i>and</i> fire breath. Or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or find a living sample and mimic that. Making your own seems like it'd be far harder than copying an existing system.<br /> <br /> Might be interesting though if you had a Mage <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/j2g90EW.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">mapping out the metaphysical anatomy of the dragon</a> so that they may assume it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://vignette3.wikia.nocookie.net/harrypotter/images/f/f5/Leaky.JPG/revision/latest?cb=20110513163607\" target=\"_blank\">Then again I like my mages to be scientists.</a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 01-23-2016, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T13:23:08-08:00","id":814997,"title":"","content":"Am I misremembering? I thought there was a bit of a Potency requirement on getting powerful forms with all murdery bits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T13:31:10-08:00","id":815002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=814997#post814997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I misremembering? I thought there was a bit of a Potency requirement on getting powerful forms with all murdery bits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I've never done it myself. No game I've been in has lasted long enough to get that far. So it's all speculation on my part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T18:31:08-08:00","id":815166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=814997#post814997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I misremembering? I thought there was a bit of a Potency requirement on getting powerful forms with all murdery bits.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There hasn't been anything like that as far as I can recall. There certainly could be a surcharge of one Potency per feature though -if- you're using Weaving instead of Patterning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T00:37:08-08:00","id":815294,"title":"","content":"I'd say that transforming into an animal that never existed would require a Making spell or a few Patterning and Weaving spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T06:14:52-08:00","id":815393,"title":"","content":"If you're transforming (Even into something that doesn't exist) I don't see why you would need more than one Patterning spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T09:45:26-08:00","id":815526,"title":"","content":"Yeah, transforming into arbitrary animals makes sense as Patterning to me rather than Making, but we're definitely getting into Interesting Magical Research here - does it need to exist before you can turn into it? What if you <i>make</i> one with Making - can you then transform into it?<br /> <br /> I'm probably confusing Weaving body-modification spells (stuff like &quot;give myself claws&quot;) with the full transformation Patterning effect to get to that potency-requirement thought. The spell does leave us very open to ST interpretation on average creature stats, too, and I'm curious how people would handle its intersection with cryptozoology...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T12:20:02-08:00","id":815615,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't require an animal to exist before a Mage can turn into it. It's magic, not mimicry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> with the full transformation Patterning effect to get to that potency-requirement thought </div> </div> </div> I don't understand this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T15:27:25-08:00","id":815717,"title":"","content":"That refers to my post on the previous page, in which I was wrong about something - I thought scarier animals (same size, bigger claws and tougher scales) needed a higher potency spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T16:43:32-08:00","id":815756,"title":"","content":"Well easily tranforming into unexisting things with made up feature feels quite broken (not much of a problem) and would give many an ST a headache (a problem). Though i won't argue about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T18:16:39-08:00","id":815792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=815717#post815717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That refers to my post on the previous page, in which I was wrong about something - I thought scarier animals (same size, bigger claws and tougher scales) needed a higher potency spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the clarification.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=815756#post815756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well easily tranforming into unexisting things with made up feature feels quite broken (not much of a problem) and would give many an ST a headache (a problem). Though i won't argue about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're a Mage ST you're setting yourself up for headaches no matter what, I don't see the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T20:58:12-08:00","id":815876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=814022#post814022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . .It's always amusing to see which Legacies people think are &quot;too esoteric to play&quot; or &quot;too boring&quot;. Wolsey's old player has recently joined my ongoing game after moving back into proximity with the rest of us, and, well... He's leaning heavily Perfected Adept.<br /> <br /> Legacies people have actually played in my games - Bearers of the Eternal Voice, House of Ariadne, Uncrowned Kings, Sphinx, two custom Legacies, Children of the Hour, Tamers of Fire, Eleventh Question, and Sisterhood of the Blessed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always thought the Sisterhood of the Blessed had a lot of story potential, in part because their (real life) counterparts are so obvious, and such a part of every day life. Taking Grandma to bridge club, and finding out that - between hands and gossiping about their grandkids - they summon demons. Or that a bunch of trophy wives on the charity circuit actually <i>are</i> plotting to take over the world. And who knows what the &quot;rich girl&quot; sorority on campus really gets into, behind closed doors?<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I don't envy you, having to write them up as a coherent group. Such a generation gap has opened up, in the last hundred years or so. . . The wealthy dowager, who's never even owned a pair of pants, and remembers both the women's suffrage movement and Amelia Earhart, is the obvious face of the Legacy. But so is her granddaughter, newly admitted to Harvard, and looking to run wild. Tough to come up with a coherent, concise description that fits both (and that's <i>before</i> you factor in the cardio striptease classes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T09:23:53-08:00","id":819835,"title":"","content":"I think we've had a lot of voices chime in on what they want to see on the Mastigos, Obrimos, and Thyrsus Legacies. Most of which I actuall agree with. I feel like we've hit kind of a rough consensus on the matter. Now, I'm wondering if I can hijack this thread for something a bit related, but different from DaveB's purpose: <br /> <br /> In the opening post, we were told that 11th Question and the Sisterhood of the Blessed will be in. Now, pretend that we weren't told that, and instead we were told that we were getting the Clavicularius/Bene Ashmedai, the Dreamspeakers, and the Perfected Adapts / Tamer of Fire. What would you consider to be iconic Legacies for the Acanthus and Moros? Curious minds inquiring. What's the iconic Legacies there? Would you keep either of them, or do you have other tastes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T10:47:33-08:00","id":819879,"title":"","content":"I'd go Daoine and Bokor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T11:39:43-08:00","id":819901,"title":"","content":"Walkers in Mists and Stone Scribes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T10:46:11-08:00","id":820434,"title":"","content":"Daoine and Uncrowned Kings (for alchemy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T11:57:56-08:00","id":820473,"title":"","content":"And the results are in. Not remotely scientific, but this isn't a democracy. <br /> <br /> The four Legacies I'll blog up after 2e's release are the Sisterhood of the Blessed, the Cryptologos, the Perfected Adepts, and the Orphans of Proteus. We have another set of five picked out for a bonus round should that turn out to not take as long as I think it will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T12:20:28-08:00","id":820496,"title":"","content":"Cryptologos? That's a surprise. I was sure we were going to get Clavicularius/Bene Ashmedai.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T13:04:59-08:00","id":820526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=820473#post820473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the results are in. Not remotely scientific, but this isn't a democracy. <br /> <br /> The four Legacies I'll blog up after 2e's release are the Sisterhood of the Blessed, the Cryptologos, the Perfected Adepts, and the Orphans of Proteus. We have another set of five picked out for a bonus round should that turn out to not take as long as I think it will.</div> </div> </div> </div>No Moros? Hmm, guess noone at your table is one. <br /> <br /> Edit:forgot Phil. Poor Phil","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T13:05:30-08:00","id":820527,"title":"","content":"The Moros is done, go look at the devblogs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T13:57:08-08:00","id":820550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=820527#post820527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Moros is done, go look at the devblogs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Took me a minute to realize you meant the 11th Question and not a new Legacy. And I got my hopes up, too!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T14:57:13-08:00","id":820577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=820473#post820473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The four Legacies I'll blog up after 2e's release are the Sisterhood of the Blessed, the Cryptologos, the Perfected Adepts, and the Orphans of Proteus. We have another set of five picked out for a bonus round should that turn out to not take as long as I think it will.</div> </div> </div> </div>That selection seems a bit strange. I think the Cryptologos are more of a Free Council Legacy than a Mastigos Legacy, so the balance feels off somehow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T15:06:54-08:00","id":820585,"title":"","content":"It turns out that a legacy can identify with a Path and an Order. Go figure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T15:08:34-08:00","id":820586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/793530-which-legacies-do-you-want-in-the-post-release-batch?p=820527#post820527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Moros is done, go look at the devblogs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, he did it for a character in his game, Phil(omedes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T15:26:52-08:00","id":820607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div cl